-- R08 — Opposite-side leans: review the open card first; no offsetting cards without an intact verdict, a dated exit and a NET line.
-- Owner request, 22 Oct 2026 (project thread "Opposite-side trade conflict rule"): the Fable digest carded P23 long NQZ26
-- (tactical, into the FOMC) while P13 short NQZ26 was open, reviewed P13 as "weakened (positioning washed out; P23 opened
-- against it)" and kept both. A view change is to be handled as an exit decision on the open card first; an opposite card
-- needs an intact verdict on the old one, a dated exit before its next review, and a printed net exposure.
-- Proposed 22 Oct 2026 from a cloud thread with this exact statement (dash.propose_rule raises no approval prompt);
-- apply_after = the next Sunday 20:00 SGT window (Sun 25 Oct 2026), when the Sunday "apply rules" task puts it in force
-- unless the owner replies "oppose R08" to the weekly review email; both digests then read it through dash.rules_in_force()
-- from the Mon 26 Oct 07:15 SGT run. Rerunning this file would propose a new rule id, so run it only to re-propose after a revert.
-- To put it in force before the Sunday window (one line in the Supabase SQL editor, project diiwqbxyhtgvozhncoef):
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R08' and status = 'proposed';
-- On a conflict the rule wins over the prompt and the trade_book_spec on that point only (STEP 1f in both prompts), so the
-- spec's TACTICAL WASHOUT sentence on opposite-direction tactical vs thematic cards is superseded without a spec edit.
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "Opposite-side leans: review the open card first; no offsetting cards without an intact verdict, a dated exit and a NET line", "body": "OPPOSITE-SIDE LEANS: REVIEW THE OPEN CARD FIRST (owner, 22 Oct 2026). A lean that runs against an open or pending card is first a decision about that card, not a new trade. Applies in both books to every candidate (thematic, tactical, hedge, re-entry) at THE TRADE TEST, before tests (a) to (f).\n\n1. SCOPE. Match the candidate against every open and pending card whose proxy is the same, or the same underlying in another wrapper (NQZ26 / ^NDX / QQQ; ^KS11 / EWY; a spot cross and its forward or NDF; the same future in another month), or whose factor label is the same with the opposite sign (a long carded under \"AI unwind\" against a short carded under \"AI unwind\"), or whose 60-session return correlation with the candidate's proxy is at or beyond +/-0.7 in the MARK SCRIPT's bars (both series are already downloaded; if it cannot be computed, say so and use the first two tests). A match in the same direction stays \"covered by Pnn\" as before.\n\n2. REVIEW FIRST. For each opposite match, review the open card now, out of cycle, to the REVIEW standards, on one question: given what makes the new lean attractive, is the open card's thesis intact, weakened or dead? Print one line in the TRADE BOOK block: \"CONFLICT: <lean> vs <Pnn direction proxy> - <intact / weakened / dead>: <reason, 20 words or fewer>\". Then:\n(i) DEAD, or WEAKENED by the same evidence that drives the new lean (\"positioning washed out\" is the new lean's thesis and the old card's weakening at once): CLOSE the open card (VIEW CHANGED, FIRST-HOUR EXIT, CHANGES and LOG lines as usual; a pending card is vetoed, \"veto Pnn\"). Then test the lean off the flat book like any candidate and card it only if it passes THE TRADE TEST on its own numbers (EV > 0 at its own REF, stop and target; thin edge tagged as usual); its card says \"replaces Pnn (closed <date>)\". The book never holds two cards that offset each other because the model changed its mind.\n(ii) INTACT, with a reason that would put the old card on again today: the old card stays, and an opposite card is allowed ONLY when it is a TACTICAL washout into a named boundary or a HEDGE (spec HEDGE TRADES), its exit falls before the old card's next review date or catalyst (print \"exit <date, time SGT>, before <Pnn> review <date>\"), and the card prints the NET line (item 3). A thematic lean opposite to an intact thematic card is never carded: TESTED records it as \"not carded (f): opposite to open Pnn - thesis intact, nets to a close\" (the 21 Oct short EURUSD against P17), and the open card's REVIEW line gains the opposing evidence.\n(iii) DEFAULT, when the review cannot say intact with a reason: close the open card and card nothing new. \"Different horizon\", \"different class\" or \"the tactical names its exit\" are not reasons on their own; a view the model would not re-enter today is dead.\n\n3. NET LINE, on every card opened against a card that stays open, repeated on both cards' rows in OPEN AND PENDING while both are open: \"NET: <long/short> <proxy> <+/-0.xxR per 1%> (<Pnew> <+/-0.xxR>, <Pold> <+/-0.xxR>) until <new card's exit>; then <Pold> alone\". A card's exposure in R per 1% move = direction x 0.01 x latest mark / its 1R in price (|entry or REF - stop|; every card is sized 1R); the net is the sum. Example, Fable 22 Oct 2026, mark 29,780: P23 long NQZ26, stop 500.5 points away, +0.59R per 1%; P13 short NQZ26, stop 867.5 points away, -0.34R per 1%; NET long NQZ26 +0.25R per 1% until the 27 Oct close, then P13 alone. The BOOK line counts the net for that factor, not two trades.\n\n4. On this point the rule supersedes the spec's TACTICAL WASHOUT sentence \"A tactical and a thematic trade on the same proxy in opposite directions are allowed only when the tactical card names the exit that reconciles them\": the reconciling exit stays necessary and is no longer sufficient; items 2 and 3 are required too.\n\n5. FIRST RUN under this rule, both books: apply item 2 to every pair of open or pending cards that already offset each other (same proxy, or the same factor label with opposite sign): print the CONFLICT line and either close the weakened card by FIRST-HOUR EXIT or keep both with the NET line, as item 2 decides; log the decision.", "rationale": "Owner, 22 Oct 2026: when the view changes, evaluate unwinding the existing trade first instead of putting on a new trade the other way. The spec's tactical-vs-thematic allowance (a reconciling exit is enough) let a view change be booked as an offsetting card with no decision on the open one and no net exposure printed.", "evidence": "Fable 22 Oct 2026: P23 NEW long NQZ26 (tactical, exits 27 Oct close, EV +0.19R) opened while P13 short NQZ26 (thematic, AI unwind, review due that day) was open; the same run's REVIEWS line read \"P13 - weakened (positioning washed out; P23 opened against it)\" and kept it to 29 Oct, the card said \"reconciled - P23 exits 27 Oct regardless, P13 keeps 30,800\" and printed no net: with stops 500.5 and 867.5 points away the book was net long NQ about +0.25R per 1% while counting two trades. P24 long EEM (factor AI unwind) opened against P13 and P10 the same day. Fable 21 Oct: \"short EURUSD ... not carded (f): opposite to open P17 - nets to a close\" with no review of P17. Opus 22 Oct: \"short Nasdaq ... not carded (c): opposes P11\" with no review of P11.", "revert_if": "Revert if, over 4 weeks, cards closed under item 2(i) or (iii) would have been in profit at their original review date in 3 or more of 4 cases (exits premature), or a weekly review finds the CONFLICT or NET line missing or mis-computed on 2 or more offsetting cards.", "supersedes": null, "review_due": "2026-12-04", "source": "owner"}$j$::jsonb);
